# Strict Python-source-only repository policy.
# Ignore everything by default, then explicitly re-allow only:
#   - this .gitignore file
#   - *.py files (in any directory, including nested ones)
*

!.gitignore
!*.py
!*/

# Explicit call-outs (already covered by the blanket "*" rule above,
# listed for clarity/documentation of intent). Root-anchored ("/name") so
# these only match the top-level directory of that name, never a same-named
# source subpackage elsewhere in the tree (e.g. src/data/ must stay tracked).
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/
/data/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Added for the checkpoint-pipeline / dashboard update ---
# The original policy above tracks only .py files. This update also ships a
# dashboard (HTML/JS/JSON), a static preview, YAML/Markdown config and docs,
# and small result files (JSON/CSV/PNG/TXT) -- none of which are .py. These
# rules re-allow exactly those new paths; they do not change what the
# original policy does to any other path (e.g. assets/, output/ at repo
# root remain governed by the rules above, untouched).
!/config/**
!/requirements.txt
!/README.md
!/documents/**
!/dashboard/**
!/preview/**
!/outputs/checkpoint_training/**
!/outputs/checkpoint_overfitting_assessment/**
!/outputs/eda_checkpoints/**

# Still excluded even inside the re-allowed paths above: trained model
# binaries, the dashboard's local SQLite history, and any raw dataset.
*.joblib
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/data/*.csv

